          Alberto Clerici
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  Imperial Motto of Frederick III (1415-1493), Holy Roman Emperor and ruler 
of Austria:
  "The whole world is subject to Austria"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the coming of the spring season Giovanna d'Arco set out to quench her 
thirst for glory.  She gathered her courage and nervously entered the 
Monastery.  Giovanna d'Arco drew out her Sword Excalibur.  She encountered 
the Witch.  Her powers magnified by the Monastery, a White Magic Place of 
Power, Giovanna d'Arco incanted the magic words for a Spiritwrack spell, but 
bit her lip on the last syllable and flubbed the spell.  Lifting her hands 
high in the air, the Witch cast a Telekinetic Storm spell and inflicted 13 
damage points.  Giovanna d'Arco dropped to the ground, mortally pierced.  
And so it came to pass that Giovanna d'Arco met her tragic end.  She was 
succeeded by her next-in-line (who will use her predecessor's name until 
next turn).  The Witch stooped to recover the belongings of Giovanna d'Arco. 
The Witch took the Sword Excalibur.

  Hakim tried a Phantasmal Armies spell, but botched it.  His Phantasmal 
Armies spell backfired and he was left covered with psycho-kinetic slime.
  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) sent an invasion force into the 
adjacent Forest province of Maplehaven, owned by Giovanna d'Arco.  Alaric 
(#22)'s forces conquered Maplehaven without any major engagements.  Alaric 
leads approximately 1 Bowmen and 2 Legion.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Giovanna d'Arco for this year.


  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Giovanna d'Arco 
treated with her ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Giovanna d'Arco treated 
with her ally Hokuto (#4).  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Prometeo 
(#5).  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally II Kahn (#6).  Giovanna d'Arco 
treated with her ally Circe (#8).  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally 
Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Tilden (#47) has just recently wandered into Bam Yanga from Abu Matariq.
  The 182nd Trolls grew tired of the whores of Pearlgate and moved on off to 
Moussoro where they hoped the entertainment would be more to their liking.
  The 183rd Trolls lost hope of finding adventure in Maicuru, and so they 
mustered their strength and moved on to Bam Yanga.


  Here is the financial report for Giovanna d'Arco's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 62 gold in revenue.  16 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  46 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Giovanna d'Arco was 
left with 31 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Rolando
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  My attempted cast of the Bless spell didn't work.
  Windy spring blossomed into a sultry early summer.  I was tutored in the 
art of Element Magic by Bairn.  I tried to practice my Element Magic, but 
the task was beyond my ability.
  With the coming of the late summer season I instructed the 177th Legion 
and the 274th Legion to remain in Pearlgate with Giovanna d'Arco.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into fall.  I levied the 20th Legion and 
the 21st Legion in Pearlgate to serve me.
  In early winter, I marched on Kajaani (#1603) with my formidable forces.

  Thy humble servant,   Rolando


From: Hakim
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I wandered far and wide in Cascadia, exploring its mysteries, 
and raising our exploration level in Cascadia to 97%.  I saw no monster.
  The wet spring blossomed into a sultry early summer.  I moved into 
Moussoro.  In my travels, I encountered no marauding monsters.
  In late summer, I journeyed to Pearlgate.  I encountered no monsters.
  With the coming of the fall season, I tried a Phantasmal Armies spell, but 
botched it.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  Hakim's Phantasmal Armies spell 
backfired and I was left covered with psycho-kinetic slime.

  Thy humble servant,   Hakim


From: Tonto, Squire to Tiffany
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Tiffany cast a Bless spell.  Moongard was magically blessed and 
prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 25th Legion were Blessed and 
permanently destroyed.  The skeletal remains of the 45th Legion were Blessed 
and permanently destroyed.  The skeletal remains of the 46th Dragons were 
Blessed and permanently destroyed.
  During early summer, Tiffany cast a Bless spell.  Pearlgate was magically 
blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Pearlgate.
  In late summer, Tiffany cast a Bless spell.  Tigerhome was magically 
blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Tigerhome.
  During fall, Tiffany's attempted cast of the Tornado spell was 
unsuccessful.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  Tiffany moved into Kajaani (#1603) 
with her army.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Tiffany


From: Drake
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I marched on Tigerhome (#1702) with my command.
  In early summer, I boldly marched my forces into Chandrapur (#1801).  I 
marched along an unusual route through Chandrapur and raised our exploration 
there to 100%.
  Midsummer's night passed and a pleasant late summer came.  I spoke to 
Adhemar of the grandness of Giovanna d'Arco's realm and convinced Adhemar to 
pledge his allegiance to Giovanna d'Arco.  After talking to Adhemar, I 
judged him (a Elf famous for Exploring) to have a Good, Cautious character.
  With the coming of the fall season I moved into Tigerhome (#1702) with my 
high-spirited army.
  In early winter, I cast a Bless spell.  Tigerhome was magically blessed 
and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Tigerhome.

  Thy humble servant,   Drake


From: Watson, Squire to Isis
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Isis rode into Pearlgate.  She saw no monster.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  Isis practiced her Element 
Magic diligently for months, but could make no significant progress.
  With the coming of the late summer season Isis practiced her Element Magic 
well but could not improve her skill in Element Magic.
  In fall, Isis's Tornado spell backfired and Isis was left with her face 
covered with psycho-kinetic slime.
  The fall season darkened into a frigid early winter.  Isis travelled to 
Kajaani.

  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Isis


From: Bairn
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I journeyed to Pearlgate.  While adventuring, I encountered no 
marauding monster.
  During early summer, I tried to practice my Element Magic, but the task 
was beyond my natural ability.
  Midsummer's day passed and late summer came.  I tried to improve my 
Element Magic, but the task was beyond my ability.
  The summer surrendered to fall.  I cast a Tornado spell.  Magical 
tornadoes hit the defenders of Kajaani.  The Tornado affected no armies in 
Kajaani.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I moved into Kajaani.

  Thy humble servant,   Bairn


From: Adhemar
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In fall, I tried to explore Chandrapur but it seemed that it had already 
been completely explored.  I discovered also that Chandrapur has been the 
site of hard-fought battles.  Many intrepid warriors have given their lives 
on its fields: the 197th Legion (Average Humans).  My efforts raised my 
skill in Exploring.  I saw no marauding monster.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I rode into Jaguardo.  I 
marched along an unusual route through Jaguardo and raised our exploration 
there to 100%.  While adventuring, I encountered no monsters.

  Thy humble servant,   Adhemar


